{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["I have explained: every supplicant who seeks what will be given to him — it is in his hand. Therefore he said: 'my hands' — two of them." "And the meaning of 'like a parched land' — just as it hopes for water, so my soul hopes for You."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 143, :notes {0 "Reading ינתן לו בידו as 'it is given to him in his hand'; the argument is compressed and the syntax is difficult."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:35.302491051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}